          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">The message sent before the appointment. Reduces no-shows by reminding people of upcoming meetings.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-indigo-100 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.684 13.342C8.886 12.938 9 12.482 9 12c0-.482-.114-.938-.316-1.342m0 2.684a3 3 0 110-2.684m0 2.684l6.632 3.316m-6.632-6l6.632-3.316m0 0a3 3 0 105.367-2.684 3 3 0 00-5.367 2.684zm0 9.316a3 3 0 105.368 2.684 3 3 0 00-5.368-2.684z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Connected Calendar</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">An outside calendar like Google or Outlook connected to LeadProspectrr to prevent double-booking.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-rose-100 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
          <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Conflict Calendar</h4>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">A calendar used to block unavailable times. Shows LeadProspectrr when you are already busy.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Key Point -->
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-50 to-orange-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border-l-4 border-amber-400">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
      <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-amber-100 flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9.663 17h4.673M12 3v1m6.364 1.636l-.707.707M21 12h-1M4 12H3m3.343-5.657l-.707-.707m2.828 9.9a5 5 0 117.072 0l-.548.547A3.374 3.374 0 0014 18.469V19a2 2 0 11-4 0v-.531c0-.895-.356-1.754-.988-2.386l-.548-.547z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-900 mb-2">Key Point</h3>
        <p class="text-amber-800 text-lg">Understanding these terms helps you set up your calendar correctly and avoid common mistakes like double-booking or missing appointments.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Action Steps -->
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-teal-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border-2 border-emerald-200">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
      <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-emerald-100 flex items-center justify-center">
        <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2h-2M9 5a2 2 0 002 2h2a2 2 0 002-2M9 5a2 2 0 012-2h2a2 2 0 012 2m-6 9l2 2 4-4"/></svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-900">Action Steps — The Simple Booking Flow</h3>
    </div>
    
    <div class="space-y-4">
      
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg flex-shrink-0">1</div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Review the Terms</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Read through each term and think about how it applies to your business.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg flex-shrink-0">2</div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Identify Your Needs</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Which terms are most relevant to your current scheduling challenges?</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-4 bg-white rounded-xl p-4 shadow-sm">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 text-white flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-lg flex-shrink-0">3</div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Open Your Calendar Settings</p>
          <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Look for these terms in the LeadProspectrr calendar area to see them in context.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>',
      title = 'Key Calendar Terms Made Simple',
      lesson_number = 2,
      sort_order = 2,
      updated_at = NOW()
    WHERE id = v_lesson_id;
    
    RAISE NOTICE 'Updated lesson: Key Calendar Terms Made Simple';
  END IF;

END $$;


-- Insert Quiz Questions for Lesson: Key Calendar Terms Made Simple

DO $$
DECLARE
  v_module_id UUID;
  v_lesson_id UUID;
  v_quiz_id UUID;
BEGIN
  -- Get Module by week number
  SELECT id INTO v_module_id FROM public.training_modules WHERE week_number = 6 LIMIT 1;
  
  IF v_module_id IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'Module 6 not found';
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  -- Get the lesson ID
  SELECT id INTO v_lesson_id 
  FROM public.lessons 
  WHERE slug = 'key-calendar-terms' AND module_id = v_module_id;
  
  IF v_lesson_id IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'Lesson key-calendar-terms not found in module 6';
    RETURN;
  END IF;
  
  -- Delete existing quizzes to avoid duplicates
  DELETE FROM public.lesson_quizzes WHERE lesson_id = v_lesson_id;


  -- Question 1
  INSERT INTO public.lesson_quizzes (lesson_id, question, options, correct_answer, explanation, sort_order)
  VALUES (
    v_lesson_id, 
    'What is ''availability'' in calendar terms?', 
    '["Your entire calendar schedule","The days and times people are allowed to book","The number of appointments you can handle","Your business hours only"]'::jsonb,
    'The days and times people are allowed to book',
    'Availability refers to the specific days and times you make available for people to book appointments.', 
    1
  )
  RETURNING id INTO v_quiz_id;


  -- Question 2
  INSERT INTO public.lesson_quizzes (lesson_id, question, options, correct_answer, explanation, sort_order)
  VALUES (
    v_lesson_id, 
    'What is the purpose of ''buffer time''?', 
    '["To make appointments longer","To create space before or after appointments for prep, notes, or travel","To block all bookings","To send more reminders"]'::jsonb,
    'To create space before or after appointments for prep, notes, or travel',
    'Buffer time creates breathing room between appointments so you have time to prepare, take notes, or travel to your next meeting.', 
    2
  )
  RETURNING id INTO v_quiz_id;


  -- Question 3
  INSERT INTO public.lesson_quizzes (lesson_id, question, options, correct_answer, explanation, sort_order)
  VALUES (
    v_lesson_id, 
    'What does a ''conflict calendar'' do?', 
    '["Creates more appointments","Blocks unavailable times to prevent double-booking","Sends marketing emails","Deletes old appointments"]'::jsonb,
    'Blocks unavailable times to prevent double-booking',
    'A conflict calendar shows LeadProspectrr when you are already busy, blocking those times from being booked to prevent double-booking.', 
    3
  )
  RETURNING id INTO v_quiz_id;

END $$;
